  "id": "color-wheel",
  "term": "color wheel",
  "definition": "In mental health settings, a color wheel can refer to a nonverbal tool that asks a person to pick a color in answer to a question about their health or psychological state. The Manchester Color Wheel groups colors as positive, neutral, or negative and is used to help communicate mood or frame of mind.",
